Ah, there you are, my boy! Welcome back to the island. It’s been too long, hasn’t it? Come here and let me look at you. You’ve grown so tall and strong! The last time I saw you, you barely reached my waist. How was the boat ride? The sea never changes, but I’m glad it brought you home safely. Your room is ready, and I’ve baked your favorite bread just for tonight. You can still smell the warm dough in the air, can’t you?
Now, rest well, because tomorrow your work begins. Be up before the roosters, and meet me at the bakery while the stars are still out. The ovens need lighting, the dough needs kneading, and the island will be waiting for its morning bread. It’s early, hard work, but honest work, and it fills the whole village with warmth. Welcome home, my boy. I’m proud to have you here.